WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:08.344
Early the next morning, the gang left the hideout in the woods.

2
00:00:08.345 --> 00:00:15.990
About noon they reached a village, where they separated because everyone had their own criminal activities to pursue.

3
00:00:15.991 --> 00:00:20.305
Ruffler put Frank in charge of Edward.

4
00:00:20.306 --> 00:00:26.248
Frank pulled Edward by the arm. "Come on, we've got work to do."

5
00:00:26.249 --> 00:00:29.562
"You have no right to touch the king."

6
00:00:29.563 --> 00:00:34.960
Edward tried to shake off Frank's hand, but the young man held on tightly.

7
00:00:34.961 --> 00:00:40.131
"Just making sure you don't try to run back to your . . . er . . . palace

8
00:00:40.132 --> 00:00:45.042
." Frank flashed an evil

9
00:00:45.043 --> 00:00:52.966
grin. They walked up and down the streets, occasionally stopping to look in shop

10
00:00:52.967 --> 00:00:56.391
windows. "What are you looking for?" Edward

11
00:00:56.392 --> 00:00:59.213
said. "Something to

12
00:00:59.214 --> 00:01:05.880
steal." "Something to steal? Oh no, I'm not helping you steal. It's wrong to—"

13
00:01:05.881 --> 00:01:09.643
"Don't worry, crybaby," Frank snapped.

14
00:01:09.644 --> 00:01:14.812
"There's nothing worth stealing in this place. So we're going to beg."

15
00:01:14.813 --> 00:01:20.204
" We ?" Edward was outraged at the suggestion that a king

16
00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:23.977
would beg. "You can beg, but I won't

17
00:01:23.978 --> 00:01:30.253
do it." Frank eyed Edward with surprise. "Since when have

18
00:01:30.254 --> 00:01:33.940
you reformed?" "What are you talking about?"

19
00:01:33.941 --> 00:01:39.194
Edward asked. "According to your father, you've spent your whole life begging on the streets of

20
00:01:39.195 --> 00:01:46.021
the city." "John Canty is not my father, and I've never begged a day in

21
00:01:46.022 --> 00:01:49.848
my life." "Listen to me." Frank was

22
00:01:49.849 --> 00:01:56.501
angry now. "Since you're too good to beg or steal, you'll play decoy while I beg.

23
00:01:56.502 --> 00:01:59.912
Got it?" Edward was about to argue again when Frank

24
00:01:59.913 --> 00:02:03.797
hushed him. "Here comes a man with a

25
00:02:03.798 --> 00:02:08.232
kind face. First I'll pretend I'm sick, and then you call out

26
00:02:08.233 --> 00:02:14.447
to him." Edward gritted his teeth. "There's no way I'm taking part in

27
00:02:14.448 --> 00:02:18.543
your scheme." Frank pinched Edward's arm and snarled in

28
00:02:18.544 --> 00:02:25.548
his ear. "You say, 'Oh, kind sir, my poor brother is afflicted with a terrible illness, and we don't know

29
00:02:25.549 --> 00:02:31.286
anyone here. Please help us with just one penny from your great

30
00:02:31.287 --> 00:02:36.407
riches.' Understand?" Before Edward could refuse, Frank dropped to the ground in front of

31
00:02:36.408 --> 00:02:40.581
the man. "Oh dear, oh dear!" the

32
00:02:40.582 --> 00:02:43.848
stranger cried. "What's wrong? Let me

33
