help you!" "I don't want to trouble you with my illness,"

34
00:02:49.103 --> 00:02:54.710
Frank said. "My brother will tell you that I'm often sick and racked

35
00:02:54.711 --> 00:03:00.499
with pain. All I ask is a penny for food, and then leave me to

36
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:04.782
my misery." "A penny? I'll give you three

37
00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:09.848
pennies!" The man fumbled in his pocket and handed the coins to

38
00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:14.431
Frank. "Now come here, lad, and help me carry your brother to the

39
00:03:14.432 --> 00:03:18.670
house—" "I'm not his brother," Edward

40
00:03:18.671 --> 00:03:22.862
interrupted. "Oh, he denies knowing his own

41
00:03:22.863 --> 00:03:27.743
brother." Frank groaned as the man bent over

42
00:03:27.744 --> 00:03:37.142
him. "We are both sick. While my illness destroys my body, his sickness eats away his

43
00:03:37.143 --> 00:03:42.024
mind." The stranger looked suspiciously from Edward to Frank and back

44
00:03:42.025 --> 00:03:48.782
again. "If he's not your brother," the man said to Edward, "then who is

45
00:03:48.783 --> 00:03:51.913
he?" "A beggar and a

46
00:03:51.914 --> 00:03:56.793
thief. While you've been giving him pennies, he's been picking your

47
00:03:56.794 --> 00:04:01.980
pocket!" The man's eyes widened in surprise, and he patted his empty

48
00:04:01.981 --> 00:04:05.954
pocket. Frank jumped up and ran away with the man in hot

49
00:04:05.955 --> 00:04:10.436
pursuit. Without wasting a second, Edward fled in the opposite

50
00:04:10.437 --> 00:04:15.808
direction. "Expecting the king to beg and steal.

51
00:04:15.809 --> 00:04:21.288
Ridiculous!" Edward kept looking back for Frank as he hurried

52
00:04:21.289 --> 00:04:30.624
along. However, as the hours passed and he grew hungry, Edward realized that he'd have to beg for

53
00:04:30.625 --> 00:04:39.018
food. He knocked on a farmhouse door, but the owner took one look at his ragged clothes and shooed him

54
00:04:39.019 --> 00:04:43.516
away. "I can manage on my own! I don't need anybody's

55
00:04:43.517 --> 00:04:47.749
charity!" Edward shouted as he walked down the farmhouse

56
00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:52.843
lane. A cow raised its head and stared after

57
00:04:52.844 --> 00:04:55.912
him. Night arrived with a damp

58
00:04:55.913 --> 00:05:02.592
chill. Edward was tired, but every time he sat down to rest, the cold penetrated his

59
00:05:02.593 --> 00:05:07.455
bones. "I have to find somewhere warm to spend the

60
00:05:07.456 --> 00:05:12.006
night." He got up and started walking again.

61
00:05:12.007 --> 00:05:17.481
At last he came to a barn, where a farmworker was finishing some chores.

62
00:05:17.482 --> 00:05:21.235
Edward waited outside, near the open door.

63
00:05:21.236 --> 00:05:27.657
By the light of the man's lantern, he spotted an empty stall and some horse blankets.

64
00:05:27.658 --> 00:05:33.145
"There's my bed!" Edward thought.

65
00:05:33.146 --> 00:05:38.169
As soon as the man left, Edward crept into the dark barn.

66
00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:44.290
He put one blanket on the ground, lay down, and pulled the other blanket over him.

67
00:05:44.291 --> 00:05:50.886
"Ugh! These blankets stink of horse, but they'll have to do."

68
00:05:50.887 --> 00:05:55.729
Edward was almost asleep when something touched his face.

69
00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.779
He sat up in alarm.

70
00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:00.377
"Who's there?" he whispered.

71
00:06:00.378 --> 00:06:02.842
No one replied.

72
00:06:02.843 --> 00:06:08.189
Edward lay down with his eyes wide open even though it was too dark to see.

73
00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:14.911
The thing reached out and touched him again!

